 "area": "retina",
 "description": "OBSERVE-AND-GROUND remote causality (block 229000): the 228 correction. Ground causes(cross,rotation) from the REAL observed before->after (perception), NOT a simulated counterfactual. Per real step the adapter mints an Observation{interact, remote_changed, cause_id, effect_kind} (all OBSERVED) \u2014 the stream IS the natural timeline. rcg_ground mints a persistent CausalFact{cause,effect,status:grounded, source:observation} + `causes` edge iff a real interact->distal-change is observed AND no Observation shows a change without interaction (the natural-timeline no-op) AND no fact exists yet. rcg_knows_and_acts reads the grounded fact and seeks the cause to operate it; rcg_pass passes. Controls: no_natural_timeline (ignores the no-op -> confabulates on coincidence), blind (never observes the effect -> never grounds). Domain-agnostic (effect kind carried from the OBSERVED attr; no cross/rotation constant). Guarded on game.ground_on==1 (default-OFF, byte-identical) + game.arm. Integer-native; no Rust; reuses 216/217 perception + 227 posit + 210 operate + 220 nav.",
 "microtheory": {
  "name": "remote_causal_ground",
  "description": "A remote-causal link is GROUNDED FROM OBSERVATION: the agent interacts for real, OBSERVES the actual before->after remote change, and mints a persistent grounded causes(cause,effect) fact \u2014 refusing when the natural timeline shows the remote thing changing on its own. The grounded fact persists and the agent acts on knowing it. Every decision is a rule; grounding is perception -> graph write."
 },
